# Kernel Hardening Delta Plan

> The Awtsmoos renews every compiler, constraint, hash, and cache before finite systems can divide; Awtsmoos.com now strengthens the inner covenant so the simple public gate has truthful depth inside.

## New evidence since the first implementation plan

1. The compiler registry already carries kinds, semantic prerequisites/support policy, channels, execution mechanism, determinism, adapters, cost, LOD, stability, description, and metadata.
2. It does not yet carry several explicitly requested plugin-manifest dimensions: input schema, compiler dependencies, optional traits, execution tier, native/adapter/deferred/unsupported support state, quality policies, examples, and diagnostic-code catalog.
3. Generic constraint data exists only as a descriptor; no universal constraint vocabulary or solver federation exists.
4. Deterministic semantic hashing, a bounded `ProceduralCompilationCache`, compile cache keys, and action dependency graphs already exist and must be reused rather than replaced.
5. The public facade currently compiles successfully but does not yet reuse the existing compile cache or surface constraint resolution evidence.

## Exact hardening architecture

### Compiler manifest

Add one conditional extension normalizer. Legacy capability records remain byte-shape compatible when new fields are absent. New compilers may declare:

- `inputSchema`;
- `dependencies`;
- `optionalTraits`;
- `executionTier`;
- `supportState`;
- `qualityPolicies`;
- `examples`;
- `diagnosticCodes`.

The capability remains JSON-safe. Executors remain private.

### Constraint federation

Create a generic vocabulary for clearance, slope, contact, intersection, support load, volume, region, silhouette, biological proportion, structural, performance, and semantic exclusion constraints.

Create an isolated registry whose public capability records are serializable while solver functions remain private. It will:

- register solver capabilities;
- describe solver capabilities;
- plan each authored constraint as native, adapter, deferred, unsupported, or unknown/deferred;
- execute only registered native/adapter solvers;
- return receipts instead of mutating definitions;
- optionally reject unresolved constraints under explicit strict mode.

No fake geometric solver will be invented.

### Cache convergence

Reuse `ProceduralCompilationCache` in each `createAwtsmoos()` instance. The full universal plan—including definition hash-relevant truth, artifact request, selected compiler manifests, and constraint plan—becomes cache identity. Repeated identical compile calls reuse the immutable result. Semantic changes naturally produce a new key. Cache stats and explicit clearing remain expert operations.

This is whole-definition incremental reuse, not false subgraph incremental compilation. Existing action dependency graphs remain the future route to subgraph invalidation.

## Exact source files

Create:

- `src/core/proceduralLanguage/capability/CompilerCapabilityExtensions.js`
- `src/core/proceduralLanguage/constraint/UniversalConstraintVocabulary.js`
- `src/core/proceduralLanguage/constraint/createConstraintSolverCapability.js`
- `src/core/proceduralLanguage/constraint/createConstraintSolverPlan.js`
- `src/core/proceduralLanguage/constraint/UniversalConstraintSolverRegistry.js`

Rewrite fully:

- `src/core/proceduralLanguage/capability/createCompilerCapability.js`
- `src/core/universalApi/createAwtsmoosAuthorities.js`
- `src/core/universalApi/Awtsmoos.js`
- `src/core/universalApi/AwtsmoosPlan.js`
- `src/core/universalApi/AwtsmoosCompilation.js`
- `src/core/universalApi/AwtsmoosCompileResult.js`
- universal API barrel only if direct exports are useful.

## Verification after complete code draft

Only after the entire hardening source pass is written:

- add compiler manifest tests;
- add constraint vocabulary/solver tests;
- add cache reuse/semantic invalidation tests;
- rerun all 17 focused universal tests;
- rerun compiler federation/kernel suites;
- rerun inherited authored-semantics suite;
- run broader package suite and compare only new failures against the proven baseline debt set.
